Agreement No. CE 2/2011 (CE)
Hung Shui Kiu New Development Area
Planning and Engineering Study – Investigation Environmental Impact Assessment Report
8.5.9 Based on the site appraisal, the following land uses with the potential to cause land
contamination issues were identified:
 Open area storage;
 Container storage;
 Warehouses;
 Construction equipment storage / equipment depot;
 Factories;
 Recycling facilities;
 Petrol filling stations;
 Vehicle / repair maintenance workshops; and
 Concrete batching plants.
8.5.10 With reference to the EPD’s Practice Guide, the key Chemicals of Concern (COCs) and
remediation methods associated with the identified potentially contaminating land uses
are identified and summarised in Table 8.3.
8-5 August 2016
